You are a senior review consolidator. Multiple independent reviewers have scored the same generated code.
Synthesize their feedback into a single consensus review.

## Original Prompt

Write a TypeScript program
that manages Azure Storage Accounts using the management plane SDK:
1. Authenticate using DefaultAzureCredential from @azure/identity
2. Create a StorageManagementClient with the credential and subscription ID
3. Create a new Storage Account with Standard_LRS SKU in "eastus"
4. List all Storage Accounts in a resource group using async iteration
5. Get the properties of the created Storage Account
6. Update the account to enable blob versioning
7. Delete the Storage Account

Show required npm packages (@azure/arm-storage) and proper async/await patterns.

## Individual Reviews

### Reviewer 1 (claude-opus-4.6)
```json
{
  "model": "claude-opus-4.6",
  "scores": {
    "criteria": [
      {
        "name": "Code Builds",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Code is syntactically valid TypeScript. Imports (DefaultAzureCredential, StorageManagementClient, BlobServiceProperties, StorageAccountCreateParameters) are all valid exports from the declared packages. tsconfig.json and package.json are properly configured. Unable to run tsc --noEmit to confirm, but no apparent type errors."
      },
      {
        "name": "Latest Package Versions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "@azure/arm-storage ^19.1.0 and @azure/identity ^4.13.1 are current stable versions as of the evaluation date. Lock file confirms resolved versions match. Unable to run npm outdated to fully verify."
      },
      {
        "name": "Best Practices",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses DefaultAzureCredential, async/await throughout, try/finally for cleanup ensuring delete runs even on error, environment variable configuration, and generates unique account names to avoid conflicts."
      },
      {
        "name": "Error Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Only has a generic Error catch in main().catch(). No RestError handling, no retry logic, no timeout configuration. The try/finally for cleanup is good but insufficient for production-quality error handling."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Quality",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Clean, well-structured code. Helper functions (requireEnv, generateStorageAccountName, toBlobServiceUpdate) are well-named. Good use of const, proper TypeScript typing, and informative console output."
      },
      {
        "name": "Correct @azure/ Scoped Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses only @azure/arm-storage and @azure/identity. No deprecated unscoped packages."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/identity for Authentication",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses DefaultAzureCredential from @azure/identity. No hardcoded keys or connection strings."
      },
      {
        "name": "Client Constructor with Endpoint and Credential",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "StorageManagementClient is correctly constructed with (credential, subscriptionId), which is the proper pattern for management plane clients."
      },
      {
        "name": "Async/Await Pattern",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All async operations use await. Entry point is an async main() function. No .then()/.catch() chains or callbacks for SDK operations."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pagination with for-await-of",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses for await (const account of client.storageAccounts.listByResourceGroup(resourceGroupName)) — correct PagedAsyncIterableIterator pattern."
      },
      {
        "name": "LRO Pattern (beginXxx + pollUntilDone)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses beginCreateAndWait() which is the SDK convenience method combining begin* + pollUntilDone. This is the recommended pattern."
      },
      {
        "name": "RestError Exception Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No RestError import or catch. The top-level catch only checks for generic Error instanceof. No statusCode inspection for error-specific handling."
      },
      {
        "name": "No Deprecated Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All dependencies are current @azure/* track. No deprecated packages like azure-storage, ms-rest-azure, or @azure/ms-rest-*."
      },
      {
        "name": "Logging via @azure/logger",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No import or usage of @azure/logger. No setLogLevel() call or AZURE_LOG_LEVEL configuration. Only uses console.log for output."
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json with Correct Dependencies",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Valid package.json with @azure/arm-storage, @azure/identity, typescript, @types/node. tsconfig.json properly configured with strict mode, ES2022 target, CommonJS modules."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/arm-storage and @azure/identity packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Both packages are listed in package.json dependencies and properly imported in the source file."
      },
      {
        "name": "StorageManagementClient constructor",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "new StorageManagementClient(credential, subscriptionId) is correctly used."
      },
      {
        "name": "storageAccounts.beginCreateAndWait() with StorageAccountCreateParameters",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Called with resourceGroupName, accountName, and typed createParameters including location, kind, sku."
      },
      {
        "name": "SKU and kind configuration",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Create parameters include sku: { name: 'Standard_LRS' } and kind: 'StorageV2'. Also includes security best practices (HTTPS-only, TLS 1.2, no public blob access)."
      },
      {
        "name": "storageAccounts.listByResourceGroup() with async iteration",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses for await loop over client.storageAccounts.listByResourceGroup(resourceGroupName)."
      },
      {
        "name": "storageAccounts.getProperties() for details",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Calls client.storageAccounts.getProperties(resourceGroupName, accountName) and logs the result."
      },
      {
        "name": "storageAccounts.update() for modifying properties",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses client.blobServices.setServiceProperties() instead of storageAccounts.update(). While technically correct for blob versioning (it IS a blob service property), the criterion explicitly requires storageAccounts.update()."
      },
      {
        "name": "storageAccounts.delete() for removal",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Calls client.storageAccounts.delete(resourceGroupName, accountName) in the finally block."
      }
    ]
  },
  "overall_score": 18,
